A||||13||FieroKyle||Thinking about selling the Fiero........||||9||
Z||000000||FieroKyle||10-27-2001||09:17 PM||||In the past week I have been thinking that I don't really think want a Fiero anymore. Yes I still love them, but for my use, I dunno if I really like to own em. I have to store it half the year and I can't take it anywhere off road. I have to make sure I baby it on gravel roads and don't abuse it. I can't drive fast or race it in town, but on back roads thats a different story.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. So much care into washing it and prepping it just to go for the weekend ride. You can have one other person with ya, and working on the engine is a ***** . Its not a super fast car either, quick, but nothing really bad. I was sorta thinking about getting something I can drive year round, something thats faster or atleast can go places in. I was thinking about a truck, jeep, old monza with a 350, old camaro, just something faster or like I said can go off road. I dunno, just thinking about it. I wish I had the money to drop the Archie special in it but I don't, and probably won't for years to come. <P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||9
Z||000001||SLYGUY||10-27-2001||09:26 PM||||Don't sell it.<P>Just move to a state where the weather can't KILL you.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Hope you make the right choice<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ViewImage.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Spektrum-87GT||10-27-2001||09:46 PM||||i've thought many times of selling mine because of the reasons you've mentioned. Its not that fast, its only a 2 seater, backroads are a real pain. then i go look at it... drive it... think of all the things you can do to them... and say i'm never selling it. just ask yourself if you would be happier with a truck or old camaro. i do love jeeps though, cherokees are great trucks and have a bulletproof powerful engine to boot(high output 4.0)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fformula88||10-27-2001||11:28 PM||||I have had the same thoughts from time to time.  I hate having to store it thru the winter.  My biggest complaint would have to be the cost of ownership for two cars!  Although the wear parts should last longer, it really sucks when my Fiero and Probe need new tires all at once, plus having to pay twice the insurance, oil changes, brakes, registration etc etc.  Its a lot of cost to own a car I get 3-5K miles on a year because I "like" it a lot.  But when I think these thoughts I only have to hop in it and take it for a spin to realize I couldn't possibly sell it.  Its just that much fun to drive.  A lot more so than my Probe which is a very good performer (handling wise anyway).<P>Actually, the only car I have driven that comes close to being as much fun to drive is my fathers Geo Tracker Convertible.  Its no Fiero, as the 1.6L engine is a bit weak, and its no sports car in handling.  But its sure tossable in traffic with very quick steering, an unbelievably small turning circle, and of course the convertable top!  Now if only GM would get wise and put the V6 from the 4-door into the convertible versions!<P>Here is what you should do... get in your Fiero and find some twisty road.  Go for a spin and you'll realize you would regret selling it!||||reg||1
Z||000004||SLYGUY||10-27-2001||11:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<P><B>  I hate having to store it thru the winter.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I couldn't imagine having to do something like that. Heck, just move. California comes to mind!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Seriously though. Run it hard through some twisties. You'd be surprised how even a guy that is good on a motorcycle will have to work to keep ahead of you. <BR>I don't need reassurance, but if I ever do that should do the trick.<P>Sly||||reg||1
Z||000005||MooCow||10-27-2001||11:57 PM||||Trust me dont sell the car man.  I was going to sell my car too.  Actually a lot of times I was going to.  I am in debt with my car still $3,500 and it cant even move!!  It is the shed and has benn in the shed for over a month now and wont come out till spring.  I only got about 7,000 miles on it till the tranny cracked and I had to put it up.  I love the car to much and have put to much time into it to sell it now.  So I just cant wait for next year when I have lots of money for it and Im just saving all my pennies right now for it.  So just keep it.  It will come around and you will love it again.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||14
Z||000006||85ZainoGT||10-28-2001||12:30 AM||||I think the only thing I would give my fiero up for would be a 98 or newer Trans Am, or a corvette, and since I dont have the money for either of those, I will have to wait til I do, but by the time I have that money, my fiero may have a 3.8sc with a 100 shot or a ls1 in it, who knows, keep it man, stick a chick in it, its all wood brotha!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!!!<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1985 White/Silver GT <BR>2.8L 4 Speed LOADED :)<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sigpic2529_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||FieroKyle||10-28-2001||12:37 PM||||Well uh, I figured out I have just been in the blues with it lately, ya know? Its been gone at the body shop 2 this year and it seems like it will run good for a few days still some $50 part goes bad in it. I went out to a couple of friend's house, and when I went to go pick up my one friend, we took his car. (86 SE 2m4) instead of the pick up truck driving. (He had me drive since he has had his lisence taken away due to too many speeding tickets  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">). I was grinning the whole way again. I will never sell my Fiero or think about again. Thanks though for guy's output. I saw a Camaro (70's) really nice for sale and a Wrangler that I could afford. I might still go look at the Camaro again. Anyways, later guys.<BR><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0PgAgVMwT!1W9RUb20vChbvv6QaE!2K1LWrFB6SxTnTchZgvIygv7Y3YwXpVdD8GeNkWpurYfoQxvNRK6j6kEmOFLoIHavbIr/Kyle-85-GT.jpg">    <P>My Fast 'n Black Car<BR>Kyle - 85' GT||||reg||10
Z||000008||BlackStang95||10-28-2001||10:57 PM||||Its been gone at the body shop 2 this year and it seems like it will run good for a few days still some $50 part goes bad in it.<P>That's part of owning an older car, any make or model (despite what idiots will tell you).<BR>Unless you do a total restoration stuff will fail.||||reg||1
Z||000009||GTMike||10-29-2001||03:11 AM||||i'm just wondering   what  parts keep breaking or going bad on your car?  my fiero is the only car i have owned.  all the rest have been jeep cj7s. 3 of them.  and if you think a fiero is bad to work on  and maintain go get your self a jeep  you will be fixing sh*t every weekend.<P>i have never had to do that to my fiero.  i just work on it  when i have saved up enough money to mod it.     getting lowerign springs in a few weeks.  then a pully then 1.6 rocke arms. then a hotter ignition.<P> <P> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||ChopTop||10-29-2001||09:58 AM||||Man I can totally relate.  We have three Fiero’s, two sit in the garage and the third one is my wife’s 88 coupe daily driver.  Which is currently down because it’s developed an intermittent stalling problem a couple weeks ago.  That leaves us with my Jeep Wrangler.  We’ve currently been talking about how much financially easier it would be if we just had two vehicles, plus with the 0% interest rates car companies are currently offering looking for a new car is really tempting.  However, it is still cheaper to throw a couple hundred dollars into her car every now and then, instead of paying around 300 bucks a month for a new car for the next five years.  <P>||||reg||1
